Subject: Cantor Prototype Graduation and Reflection Loop P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 8b53fe4a-76da-4748-a990-cfbbde4aae46
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Prototype_Graduation_And_Reflection_Loop_P0.sop

& [Problem] is architecture breadth and release-grade governance obscuring the smallest executable proof

& [Decision] is a lean specification-graduation policy and one real vertical loop
  + source precedes a feature flowchart
  + the flowchart precedes typed execution
  + typed execution precedes implementation
  + live evidence precedes promotion

& [Leverage] is joining two already-proven seams
  + the existing isolated llama.cpp probe proves structured call then second-pass import
  + the current EVO-X2 MCP adapter proves verified route_attention and compact AttentionFrame output
  + the P0 tests whether a real Cantor result can replace a fixture inside that loop

& [Counterposition] is to first generalize a full runtime IDE procedure language or shared-inference engine
  + [rejection] those surfaces add breadth without increasing the present seam's falsifiability

& [RiskControl] is closed scope typed faults refusal visibility read-only effects ephemeral adapter execution private-field sanitization and experimental authority

& [Conclusion] is the P0 is the lowest-cost test of Cantor as an inference coprocessor and is justified for isolated implementation
